#X text 20 570 THE list trim IS LOAD-BEARING. list split hands the level out as a one-element list \, and route matches a SELECTOR \, not a list's first element -- so without the trim \, route warn fail rejects every alert and the TTL keeps whatever it had., f 46;
#X text 420 570 The level is stored BEFORE trimming \, because the display wants it as an atom to print and route wants it as a selector to match. Same value \, two shapes \, and Pd will not let one stand in for the other., f 46;
#X text 820 440 warn 2 s \, fail 4 s. Long enough to read one short line \, short enough not to wreck a set. Errors always time out -- a stuck error covering the display mid-performance is the worse failure., f 46;
