#X text 20 580 This draws to screen 3 \, the buffer already on show \, rather than the ALERT buffer plan-v02.md suggested. There is nothing underneath to preserve: the frame is cleared and rebuilt from stored state ten times a second \, so when the TTL expires the next frame is the meters again. Buffer 4 stays unverified -- see plan-display.md., f 58;
