#X obj 760 220 s \$0-meters-small;
#X text 20 420 plan-display.md says a moving knob shrinks the meters into a CORNER. A corner meter at 128x64 is about 40 px wide and 4 px tall \, which is less readable than a full-width 5 px strip -- and 24px text is about 18 px per character \, so the value wants the full width anyway. The intent is kept: the meters never vanish \, the parameter gets the screen., f 58;
#X text 20 570 The value and its unit arrive as one list \, so a parameter with no unit simply draws one word. See pd param-in for why they must be written together., f 58;
