#X text 20 430 Each text line is a geometry message box -- x \, y \, height -- with the words appended from a receive. pd text-out turns that into gPrintln with a typetag that fits., f 46;
#X text 420 430 The footer holds whatever u_init last reported as boot. From Phase 4 it is the obvious place for mode and tempo \, which is why it is a line of its own rather than something squeezed beside a meter., f 46;
#X text 820 430 Ten OSC messages a frame including the clear and the flip \, against six for the Phase 1 display. The metro period is one number in the parent if the device ever objects., f 46;
#X text 20 560 y 0-7 readout \, 10-21 bar \, 23-25 gate mark \, 27-34 readout \, 37-48 bar \, 50-52 gate mark \, 54-61 footer. 62 of the 64 rows \, and only because the info bar is off -- see plan-display.md., f 58;
