#X obj 1620 470 print oled-text-arity;
#X text 20 850 THE SPIGOT IS THE COLD-START GUARD. A line with no words at all -- a field that was cleared and never written -- would otherwise emit gPrintln with NO TYPETAG at all \, which packOSC reads as garbage. The word count is taken from the whole incoming list \, which always exists \, and not from the words \, which may not., f 46;
#X text 420 850 t l l l fixes the order: count the words \, stash the words \, and only then let the x/y/height head run through and collect them. Relying on which outlet an object happens to fire first is exactly what the trigger rule exists to stop., f 46;
#X text 820 850 clip 0 4 caps the text at four words in the SAME place the typetag is chosen \, so cap and tag can never disagree. list split 4 does the matching truncation -- both its left outlet and its too-short outlet \, because only the third fires when the list is shorter than the split point., f 46;
#X text 1220 850 Result: sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiiss 3 2 12 24 1 43 % -- five ints \, then one tag letter per word. Count them \; packOSC does \, and drops the message with an error you cannot see if they disagree., f 46;
