#X text 1020 360 The gate marks live with the meters they annotate: a gBox from the measured noise floor (18-19 \, x 23) to the top of a sensible gate window (25-30 \, x 38). One message \, and it reads as a zone -- below this \, it is noise -- rather than two anonymous ticks., f 46;
#X text 20 420 The coordinates are literal and visible in the message box \, which is the point -- this IS the layout \, not a call to something else that knows the layout. env~'s 0-100 became pixels back in pd levels., f 58;
#X connect 1 0 4 0;
#X connect 2 0 5 1;
